 "title": "Histone Methylation and Cardiovascular Disease Pathways",
 "summary": "This cluster is centered around the relationship between histone methylation and cardiovascular disease (CVD). Histone methylation, catalyzed by the Dot1 protein, is inhibited by H3K36 and H3K79 methylation. CVD is indicated by the accumulation of SAH, which is also inhibited by histone methylation. Drosophila melanogaster is used as a model organism to study histone methylation and its relationship to CVD. The cluster also includes various methods and tools used in the analysis, such as Western blot analysis, Polyacrylamide gel electrophoresis, and NMR spectroscopy.",
